WEBVTT

00:00.616 --> 00:01.945
Work keeps waiting.

00:02.067 --> 00:03.567
Would another app help?

00:03.688 --> 00:05.942
Nepsis first follows
the invoice to find

00:05.992 --> 00:07.748
what is actually holding it up.

00:09.228 --> 00:10.429
The job is complete.

00:10.593 --> 00:12.676
The invoice waits
for final timesheets,

00:12.726 --> 00:14.481
then review, then release.

00:14.558 --> 00:17.409
A new software box lands
beside the same gap,

00:17.459 --> 00:19.685
but nobody owns the
missing handoff.

00:21.165 --> 00:23.889
Sometimes the right
answer is a tool. First,

00:23.939 --> 00:26.398
define who supplies
the last information,

00:26.456 --> 00:28.497
by when, who checks it, and what

00:28.547 --> 00:29.918
happens when it is late.

00:31.589 --> 00:34.099
Choose the tool after
you know the bottleneck.

00:34.149 --> 00:36.201
That is the Nepsis approach.
